WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.992
The Liao cavalry formed neat ranks and advanced southward.

00:00:05.342 --> 00:00:10.214
Hoofbeats sounded, and the banners fluttered in the wind.

00:00:10.564 --> 00:00:14.860
In the Song court, the ministers were arguing heatedly.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:20.850
The minister Kou Zhun firmly urged the emperor to lead the campaign in person.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.456
The young Emperor Zhenzong of Song decided to lead the troops himself and set out northward.

00:00:26.806 --> 00:00:31.486
The grand ceremonial procession crossed mountains and rivers and arrived at the front line.

00:00:31.836 --> 00:00:35.868
The Song and Liao armies faced each other across the great river.

00:00:36.218 --> 00:00:39.770
Both sides had swords drawn and crossbows raised; the atmosphere was very tense.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.032
The two states sent envoys, who negotiated inside the camp tent.

00:00:44.382 --> 00:00:48.990
In the year 1005, the two sides signed the Chanyuan Treaty.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:54.164
From then on, peace returned to the border, and the people lived and worked in contentment.

00:00:54.514 --> 00:01:02.866
Farmers farmed in peace of mind, the markets bustled, and white doves flew in the morning light.

